# Every text file in Keys is LF in the repository, and LF in the working tree.
#
# This exists because of one commit. 2026-08-02's docs sweep (eaa283e) re-saved five
# source files and several docs as CRLF while changing 38 lines of comments in them,
# which rendered as a ~13,000 line diff over a ~490 line change: a review that cannot
# be read is a review that does not happen, and every branch open at the time was put
# into conflict with it. Nothing here is a style preference. It is the thing that stops
# a whitespace flip from hiding the change it is riding with.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text; `eol=lf` is what makes a Windows editor's
# CRLF save normalise on the way in rather than landing in a commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never inspects or converts them.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.pdf  binary
*.wav  binary
*.aiff binary
*.vst3 binary
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary
*.onnx binary
